RECONSTRUCTION - TYPE-ERASURE MODEL
→ 005.1 → Programming Language Theory

TYPE
  Dyadic erasure     : binary relation loss
  Triadic re-lifting : ternary reconstruction

VARIABLES
  structure          : must remain preserved
  initial_conditions : must be explicitly declared
  assumptions        : must be explicitly declared
  implicit           : does not exist
  flux               : generates all remaining elements

FUNDAMENTALS
  Repair works upward only if structure is preserved.
  Dyadic erasure is not equivalent to triadic re-lifting.
  Reconstruction succeeds only when initial conditions
  and assumptions are declared.
  In this system nothing is implicit:
  if it is not declared, it does not exist.
  Flux generates the rest.
